# Nissan Micra K14 five-door hatchback, 2017-2023.
#
# The Renault Flins-built fifth-generation Micra: the lower, longer car with
# the concealed rear door handle in the black C-pillar, the V-motion grille
# and the floating roof. Five-door only. UK sales from March 2017; the car
# left European catalogues at the beginning of July 2023.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Micra
#
# Dimensions 3.999 x 1.743 x 1.455 m, wheelbase 2.525 m (Nissan technical
# data sheet, 05/01/2017).
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is a true level side elevation of the Energy Orange
# launch car on the Paris 2016 stand, within about 3-5 degrees of perpendicular
# and square enough to scale from.
#
# Colours: grade (b), the Nissan GB launch release of 30 March 2017: seven
# named colours including White, Enigma Black, Platinum Silver and Passion
# Red. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39, provisional.
#
# Speed 180 km/h. Comfort 70/435, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 70. Classes 0,1.
# Dates: intro March 2017; retire staggered 2039-2042 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-micra-k14.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-micra-k14.dae. References:
# citycars/references/nissan-micra-k14/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the side photograph is slightly oblique; the wheelbase
# and overhangs use the published values. The shoulder pressing, lamp internals,
# wheel spokes and rear badges are simplified. One pre-facelift body represents
# the run.


